{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Now you shall gather, O daughter of a troop</b> — an expression of taunting. The meaning: the assembly of the troop that laid siege to Jerusalem, and they were striking the judge of Israel in their land. But what seems correct to me: that the judge of Israel is the Messiah or Zerubbabel; therefore after it: <b>And you, Bethlehem Ephrathah</b>. And Scripture speaks according to their thinking, as in \"they divide my garments among them,\" and it writes of Balak \"and he fought with Israel,\" because he said: \"perhaps I will be able to fight against him\" — and he did not fight, yet Scripture speaks only according to his thinking, as it says: \"perhaps I will be able to fight against him.\" Likewise \"the men pursued after them to the Jordan,\" while the spies were still in Jericho."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The verse reference in the title is given as Micah 4:14, following the Hebrew verse numbering; in English Bibles this is Micah 5:1."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:56.814590348Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}